  "proof_supplied": [
    "Explicit inversion-reflection across the sphere yields the full finite-p strong Neumann estimate; actual polynomial solutions and completion establish surjectivity, not assumed weak-to-strong regularity.",
    "Riesz-symbol first-order estimate, explicit one-form inversion reflection, ball kernel elimination and Rellich contradiction prove normal Hodge estimate; criticalL4 nonlinearity is absorbed.",
    "Exact exponential remainder, cancellation of contracted derivative of the Coulomb coefficient, mean-zero compatibility of every forcing, and actual strong Neumann solve give contraction independent of higher coefficient norms.",
    "Radial gauge is constructed by convergent ordered-integral series. Curvature-controlled dilation path starts at zero; a priori Hodge improvement gives a uniform critical margin. Transported perturbation bounds give a uniform positive step; finite induction reaches original connection.",
    "Constructed Neumann inverse upgrades gauge regularity to every finiteW2,p. Given finite orthogonal/constant-conjugation equivariance is preserved, including PU2 conjugation actions without SU2 representation lifts. Existing local transition data transform to continuousW2,3loc cocycles pointwise."
  ],
  "exact_hypotheses": "Smooth su2 connections on closed Euclidean four-balls; small criticalL2 curvature; Frobenius coefficient norms; homogeneous normal condition encoded by strong smooth-normal approximation; fixed finite orthogonal action with constant unitary-conjugation target action; given smooth transition maps for overlap conclusion.",
  "not_assumed": [
    "Given-smallL4 original potential",
    "Unproved Neumann/Hodge inverse",
    "Compactness closure in the parameter path",
    "Boundary Schauder theorem",
    "Global trivialization from local transition compatibility"
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "No nonsmooth starting connection or removable singularity theorem.",
    "No general curved-metric or nonconstant-lift equivariant gauge construction.",
    "No ASD Fredholm theory, perturbative transversality, gluing, orientation, Floer compactification or full surgery/nonvanishing theorem supplied."
  ],
  "original_full_claims": "All rich original97/98 Statements preserved, original five cleanup and earlier four analytic helpers frozen unchanged. Main instanton/unknot/PropertyP/GordonLuecke obligations remain held.",
  "smallest_next_prerequisite": "Bounded-curvature local gauge extraction with actual bundle/transition compactness on fixed compact domains, then singular/curved/ASD elliptic foundation; avoid treating compatible overlaps alone as global compactness.",
